# Settings of this machine. Copy to sc-turbo.conf (kept out of git) and change what differs;
# every line is optional, and the same names in the environment win.

# The Wine prefix Star Citizen is installed in. The LUG Helper's default:
#SC_PREFIX="$HOME/Games/star-citizen"

# The script that starts the game through Wine. Default: the LUG Helper's sc-launch.sh in the prefix.
#SC_LAUNCH="$SC_PREFIX/sc-launch.sh"

# That script is never changed: every launch starts a copy of it (logs/launch/) with this project's
# settings placed before the line that starts the game. Among them are the NVIDIA settings of the
# LUG wiki's Nvidia page, each only where the script or the environment has not set it: the driver's
# shader cache (on, 10 GiB, not cleaned at start), "DLSS 4" (NVIDIA's updater and the override that
# makes the game use the current DLSS with its newest preset), and a limit on the graphics memory
# the game is told about (12 GB card: 9216 MiB, 10: 8192, 8: 6144, 6: 4096, 4: 2048).
# To leave all of them out:
#SC_NVIDIA_FLAGS=0
# To leave out DLSS 4 only (the game then uses the DLSS it came with):
#SC_DLSS_OVERRIDE=0
# No memory limit, or one of your own in MiB:
#SC_VRAM_LIMIT=off
#SC_VRAM_LIMIT=10240
# Environment settings of your own for the game, which win over the script's (no spaces in a value):
#SC_LAUNCH_SET="NAME=value OTHER=value"
# Another Wine runner for the game: the folder that holds bin/wine.
#SC_RUNNER="$SC_PREFIX/runners/NAME"
# To start the launch script itself, with nothing placed:
#SC_LAUNCH_COPY=0

# The display the game runs on and its refresh rate are asked of the desktop at every launch
# (KDE Plasma, COSMIC: "sc-turbo displays"). To name them instead:
#SC_MONITOR=HDMI-A-1
#SC_FG_TARGET=120

# MangoHud at every launch with frame generation ("sc-turbo fg N hud" does it for one launch).
# It sits below the layer, so its frame rate counts the generated frames too.
#SC_MANGOHUD=1

# A sched_ext CPU scheduler while the game runs ("sc-turbo fg N sched=lavd" does it for one launch;
# needs scx-scheds, scx-tools and the polkit rule of "tools/sc-sched rule", see the README).
#SC_SCHED=lavd
